hi my name is lindsey paschall  and i'm on cornell cooperative  extension's harvest new york team i will  be discussing the supply chain for  industrial hemp  in new york state with discussions about  state of processors a little bit about  retailers and consumers  in may 2020 a survey was sent out to the  hemp processors  in new york state to find out what the  state of hemp  processing happened in 2019 out of a  little over a hundred  processors in new york state only 24  responded  13 said that they did process hemp in  new york state  and 11 said that they did not  we asked how much hemp did you process  in 2019  11 respondents did not process any hemp  and then the hemp range between zero  and twenty eight thousand two hundred  and seventy eight pounds  with a total of hundred twenty two  thousand and eighty eight pounds  processed in your state according to the  respondents  in 2019 we asked what the minimum  cbd content that hemp process required  from their growers it ranged anywhere  from 0 to 12 percent  of cbd percentage they would like from  growers  then we asked processors what they were  processing hemp into  this included hemp oil seed cake  biofuel plastic raw materials hemp fiber  pellets and that was for pellet stoves  extracts such as powders base oil  protein tinctures flour and cbd  in 2020  we wanted to know what processors were  looking at for their capacity  for processing hemp and you know the  range is  kind of all of the board but included um  weekly basis of 200 pounds um some  processors said  for a month they could only do about two  acres  or anywhere between a thousand and 140  000 pounds with also some processors  responding that they could  do anywhere from six thousand to a  million pounds  within the year  there's not a lot of information out  there in new york state about the state  of  retailers and consumers this will  probably be  potentially a future survey for to find  out from  retailers consumers where the industry  is  there's a lot of predictions on line  about how  retail stores might end up closing  because of cobit 19  you know a lot of people can buy cbd  locally  or they can buy it online so the retail  side is very unpredictable  and so is on the consumer side there's  large predictions that  cbd consumption will continue to  increase between 2020 and 2024  if you have any other questions about  hemp processors in your state  please feel free to reach out to me my  email address  is lep67 cornell.edu
 

